 "caps": [
  {
   "sec": "hook",
   "t": 0.0,
   "end": 29.178,
   "text": "Black holes: places in the universe where not even light can escape",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 6.282
  },
  {
   "sec": "hook",
   "t": 6.282,
   "end": 29.178,
   "text": "At the heart of the Milky Way sits a black hole...",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 9.962
  },
  {
   "sec": "hook",
   "t": 9.962,
   "end": 29.178,
   "text": "...as heavy as about 4 million Suns",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 13.898
  },
  {
   "sec": "hook",
   "t": 13.898,
   "end": 29.178,
   "text": "And when two black holes collided...",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 18.752
  },
  {
   "sec": "hook",
   "t": 18.752,
   "end": 29.178,
   "text": "...for an instant they released more power than all the stars in the universe",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 23.49
  },
  {
   "sec": "hook",
   "t": 23.49,
   "end": 29.178,
   "text": "But their story begins... on a battlefield",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 29.478
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 29.494500000000002,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "DECEMBER 1915",
   "big": true,
   "t1": 33.222
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 33.222,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "On the Russian front, a German army lieutenant...",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 36.624
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 36.624,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "...worked out the paths of artillery shells",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 40.107
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 40.107,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "His name was Karl Schwarzschild...",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 43.068
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 43.068,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "One of Germany's most famous astronomers",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 46.98
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 46.98,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "Amid the noise of war...",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 52.332
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 52.332,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "EINSTEIN'S GENERAL RELATIVITY",
   "big": true,
   "t1": 53.667
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 53.667,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "...he found the first exact solution of its equations",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 56.755
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 56.755,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "Einstein himself was amazed",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 58.601
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 58.601,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "But the solution hid a strange boundary",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 61.597
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 61.597,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "If all of an object's mass is squeezed into a small ball...",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 66.6
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 66.6,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "...nothing can ever come back out of it",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 69.607
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 69.607,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "Not even light",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 70.838
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 70.838,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "For the Sun, that ball would be just 6 km wide",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 74.541
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 74.541,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "For Earth, the size of a marble",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 77.165
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 77.165,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "Five months later, Schwarzschild was dead",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 80.811
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 80.811,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "He never knew what his calculation was hiding...",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 87.811
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 88.55000000000001,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "BLACK HOLE",
   "big": true,
   "t1": 89.94300000000001
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 89.94300000000001,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "More than 100 years later...",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 92.614
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 92.614,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "2026",
   "big": true,
   "t1": 94.76100000000001
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 94.76100000000001,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "The James Webb Space Telescope found a black hole...",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 99.08000000000001
  },
  {
   "sec": "cold_open",
   "t": 99.08000000000001,
   "end": 102.41300000000001,
   "text": "...that may be older than its own galaxy",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 102.71300000000001
  },
  {
   "sec": "fact10",
   "t": 107.11300000000001,
   "end": 163.584,
   "text": "But the idea was even older than Schwarzschild",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 109.67500000000001
  },
  {
   "sec": "fact10",
   "t": 109.67500000000001,
   "end": 163.584,
   "text": "1783",
   "big": true,
   "t1": 113.668
  },
  {
   "sec": "fact10",
   "t": 113.668,
   "end": 163.584,
   "text": "The village priest of Thornhill, England...",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 115.247
  },
  {
   "sec": "fact10",
   "t": 115.247,
   "end": 163.584,
   "text": "...John Michell",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 117.03500000000001
  },
  {
   "sec": "fact10",
   "t": 117.03500000000001,
   "end": 163.584,
   "text": "...wrote a long letter to his friend Henry Cavendish",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 120.49600000000001
  },
  {
   "sec": "fact10",
   "t": 120.49600000000001,
   "end": 163.584,
   "text": "Michell also studied earthquakes...",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 123.131
  },
  {
   "sec": "fact10",
   "t": 123.131,
   "end": 163.584,
   "text": "...and his balance was later used to weigh the Earth",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 128.181
  },
  {
   "sec": "fact10",
   "t": 128.181,
   "end": 163.584,
   "text": "Using Newton's gravity, he asked a simple question",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 132.245
  },
  {
   "sec": "fact10",
   "t": 132.245,
   "end": 163.584,
   "text": "What if a star were as dense as the Sun...",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 134.996
  },
  {
   "sec": "fact10",
   "t": 134.996,
   "end": 163.584,
   "text": "...but 500 times wider?",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 138.329
  },
  {
   "sec": "fact10",
   "t": 138.329,
   "end": 163.584,
   "text": "The answer was shocking",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 140.11700000000002
  },
  {
   "sec": "fact10",
   "t": 140.11700000000002,
   "end": 163.584,
   "text": "Even light would be too slow to escape its gravity",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 145.71699999999998
  },
  {
   "sec": "fact10",
   "t": 145.71699999999998,
   "end": 163.584,
   "text": "Such a star would be completely invisible",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 148.411
  },
  {
   "sec": "fact10",
   "t": 148.411,
   "end": 163.584,
   "text": "Michell called them...",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 149.69899999999998
  },
  {
   "sec": "fact10",
   "t": 149.69899999999998,
   "end": 163.584,
   "text": "DARK STARS",
   "big": true,
   "t1": 150.976
  },
  {
   "sec": "fact10",
   "t": 150.976,
   "end": 163.584,
   "text": "They could be found only by the stars orbiting them",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 157.954
  },
  {
   "sec": "fact10",
   "t": 157.954,
   "end": 163.584,
   "text": "About 200 years later, astronomers did exactly that",
   "big": false,
   "t1": 163.88400000000001
  }
 ],
